# Environment for the scripts in scripts/. Copy to .env (gitignored) at the repo root:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Each script loads .env itself. A value set in .env WINS over the same variable given
# on the command line, so keep only what never changes between runs in here. The
# per-run variables further down (TARGET, CONTRACT, PROXY, the *_ADDR ones, …) are
# listed for reference and are safer passed on the command line:
#
#   TARGET=all ./scripts/deploy.sh
#   CONTRACT=AppRegistry PROXY=0x… ./scripts/upgrade.sh
#
# The per-run variables are commented out on purpose: left in as `NAME=`, an empty
# line here blanks the value given on the command line. The same name appears under
# more than one script, and the LAST assignment in the file is the one that counts.
#
# Everything else commented out below shows its default. Never commit a real key.

# ── Every script ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required. The key that signs: the deployer for deploy.sh, the contract's admin for
# upgrade.sh, migrate.sh and set_subscription_fee.sh. There is no default.
PRIVATE_KEY=

# The chain to act on.
RPC_ENDPOINT=https://sepolia-rollup.arbitrum.io/rpc

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── deploy.sh ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which implementation to deploy: solidity (behind an upgradeable proxy) or stylus.
IMPL=solidity

# What to deploy: all | app-registry | data-registry | settlement. Prompts if unset.
# Per run.
# TARGET=

# The admin every new contract is created with: fees, takedowns and upgrades. The
# deploy's wiring calls are admin-only, so this must be the address of PRIVATE_KEY.
ADMIN_ADDR=0xB2F5361DBEF0715E1d6aa072284255dD7f1d43FC

# DataRegistry: what register() costs, in wei.
REGISTRATION_FEE=0

# AppRegistry: what claiming or renewing an app costs, in USDC base units (6
# decimals: 5000000 is 5 USDC). If non-zero, the deployer needs that much USDC to
# claim the default app.
SUBSCRIPTION_FEE=0

# The app the deployer claims right after deploying an AppRegistry: its name (the app
# id is keccak256 of it), the sha256 of its publisher terms, where they are served,
# and its join fee in wei. An empty terms hash is refused: the app could not be joined.
DEFAULT_APP_NAME=fangorn
DEFAULT_APP_TERMS_HASH=0x9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08
DEFAULT_APP_TERMS_URI=https://fangorn.network/terms.html
DEFAULT_APP_JOIN_FEE=0

# Contracts the registries call. The defaults are the Arbitrum Sepolia deployments.
USDC_ADDR=0x75faf114eafb1BDbe2F0316DF893fd58CE46AA4d
SEMAPHORE_ADDR=0x8A1fd199516489B0Fb7153EB5f075cDAC83c693D

# TARGET=app-registry only: the existing DataRegistry the new AppRegistry sits in
# front of. Required for that target (prompts if unset). Per run.
# DATA_REGISTRY_ADDR=

# TARGET=data-registry only: the existing AppRegistry to wire the new DataRegistry
# to. Required for that target (prompts if unset). Per run.
# APP_REGISTRY_ADDR=

# IMPL=stylus only: max fee per gas for `cargo stylus deploy`, in gwei.
MAX_FEE=0.1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── upgrade.sh ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required, per run. Which contract, and the address of its proxy (the address
# deploy.sh printed). Pass these on the command line: a PROXY left in here would be
# used for every upgrade, whatever the command line says.
# CONTRACT=
# PROXY=

# Optional calldata to run on the new implementation in the upgrade transaction, for
# an upgrade that has to set up new state. Per run.
# INIT_DATA=0x

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── migrate.sh ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required, per run. The NEW contracts to copy state into. If DATA_REGISTRY_ADDR is
# the old DataRegistry, that half is skipped. (deploy.sh reads these two names too,
# with a different meaning: see above.)
# APP_REGISTRY_ADDR=
# DATA_REGISTRY_ADDR=

# The contracts being migrated away from. The defaults are the Stylus deployment.
OLD_APP_REGISTRY=0x11d228c4774af3d9cae3b4b6874a12576a1a83ec
OLD_DATA_REGISTRY=0x775026e905d7b58b34d16bcbd385fa630ee36c26

# Where the old contracts live. Defaults to RPC_ENDPOINT; set it when rehearsing, to
# read from Sepolia while writing to a local chain.
# OLD_RPC_ENDPOINT=

# Where to start reading the old contracts' logs, and the widest block range one
# eth_getLogs call may span (the public Arbitrum RPC refuses more).
FROM_BLOCK=311600000
LOG_WINDOW=10000000

# A wallet to leave behind because its key is lost or compromised. Nothing it owns is
# carried over: not its publisher registration, its namespace heads, the apps it owns,
# or its memberships. An app it owned that the new contract already has (the default
# app, claimed by deploy.sh for the new admin) keeps its new owner. Optional.
# RETIRED_WALLET=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── set_subscription_fee.sh ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AppRegistry to set the fee on. Prompts if unset. The fee itself is the script's
# argument, in USDC: ./scripts/set_subscription_fee.sh 5
# APP_REGISTRY_ADDR=

# layout.sh reads no environment variables.
